      "content": "okay, i get what you're saying about the lack of a target in post 1. \n\nbut i want to dig a bit deeper into how we define \"actionable.\" what if we had a post that used that same slang/vernacular but was actually being quite aggressive? for example, if someone said \"all these [slur/group] people are just bringing the vibe down, we gotta get 'em out\" \n\nif the slang is used to deliver a hateful message, does the \"low-effort\" style make it less toxic in your eyes, or does the language itself change how you weigh the severity of the harassment? i'm trying to see if the dialect itself affects how much \"weight\" you give the sentiment.",
